  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">End-Users Stabilization Tariffs 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On August 2, 2022, Law No. 21,472 (the &quot;MPC Act&quot;), which creates the Tariff Stabilization Fund (the &quot;Fund&quot;) and establishes a New Transitional Electricity Price Stabilization Mechanism for Customers subject to Price Regulation, was published in the Official Gazette of the Republic of Chile. The MPC Act regulates the terms and conditions under which electricity tariffs are to be stabilized and paid in the future. The Fund is intended to pay the differences that may arise between invoicing by distribution companies (&quot;DisCos&quot;) to end customers for the energy and power component, and the amount payable to generation companies (&quot;GenCos&quot;) for the supply of electricity under the contractual conditions in force.</narrative>
  </description>
